FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-multiclass arms=cpu,gpu metric=devices delta=2.000000 reason=AMD box: CPU arms run for libraries with no AMD GPU path, on all cores (CONTRIBUTING.md (Comparing against libraries without a GPU path)); every arm name carries its device
FSPEED-CTR-TRACE lane=gbdt-multiclass MOJOLEARN_CTR_TRACE=1 (the fit prints its CTR config split and prep marker; DEVIATION 2634 is observable)
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-multiclass arms=* metric=mismatch delta=1.000000 reason=grower: ours and CatBoost fit MultiClass on symmetric trees (ours has no other policy for a multiclass loss); XGBoost depthwise at depth 8, LightGBM leaf-wise capped at depth 8 and 256 leaves, because neither has an oblivious grower
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-multiclass arms=* metric=mismatch delta=2.000000 reason=model shape: ours and CatBoost grow ONE tree per round with a vector of class values in each leaf; XGBoost and LightGBM grow one tree PER CLASS per round, so the fit verdict divides their tree and leaf counts by n_classes
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-multiclass arms=* metric=mismatch delta=3.000000 reason=the loss is the same softmax cross-entropy on every arm; gbm-bench itself gives CatBoost MultiClassOneVsAll beside XGBoost multi:softmax, two different losses, so the board keeps one loss on every arm
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-multiclass arms=* metric=mismatch delta=4.000000 reason=LightGBM min_child_samples 20 and min_child_weight 1e-3 stay at its defaults: at 0 (the gbdt lanes' value) LightGBM 4.7.0 aborts the first multiclass tree
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-multiclass arms=* metric=objectives delta=4.000000 reason=catboost MultiClass; lightgbm multiclass; mojolearn MultiClass; xgboost multi:softprob
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-multiclass arms=ours metric=devices delta=2.000000 reason=devices=cpu,gpu (explicit); AMD box: an opponent with an AMD GPU path runs on the GPU, one without runs on this box's CPU on all cores (CONTRIBUTING.md (Comparing against libraries without a GPU path)); the arm name says which
